 "tier1Summary": "Pressure is building on several fronts at once. Iran keeps the Strait of Hormuz closed: the [[p:Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps|IRGC]] {{note: Iran's ideological armed force, set up in 1979 after the revolution on Ruhollah Khomeini's orders.}} claims two more supertankers hit mines, Brent passed $117, and the WSJ reports a US carrier rearming for possible new strikes. [[p:Houthis|Houthi]] {{note: Zaydi Shia movement that began in northern Yemen in the 1990s under Hussein al-Houthi.}} missiles targeted Riyadh, Taif and Yanbu.\n\nDiplomacy on Ukraine is reviving. The Kremlin says trilateral talks will be held in Abu Dhabi in the first half of November, and a local ceasefire in Oleshky starts on 27 Oct. The EU wants a seat at the table but is divided: Hungary blocked Ukraine's next accession clusters, and Trump's Russian diesel deal is moving its first cargo.\n\nIn Europe, cost-of-living protests brought 410,000 people onto French streets and French 10-year bond yields passed 5%. Serbia, Bulgaria and Brazil vote today.",
